    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151-a1-a2">

                <pb facs="0285" n="243" xml:id="pg243"/>

                <head>Lord Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 3, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to my letter of the 31st
                    ultimo I have the honor to inform you that the secretary of state for the home
                    department has instructed the mayor of Liverpool to cause immediate inquiries to
                    be made with the view of ascertaining whether the Alexandra, denounced by you in
                    your letter of the 30th ultimo, is being equipped, furnished, fitted out, or
                    armed, with the intention of her being employed in the service of the so-called
                    Confederate States, with intent to commit hostilities against the federal
                    government of the United States; and, if this should appear to be the case, the
                    mayor is further instructed to adopt whatever steps can legally be taken in the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, &amp;c, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
